A||||3||loafer87gt||Protecting your computer||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||01-16-2001||08:45 PM||||After reading about MonkeyMans bad luck, I was just wondering what all safeguards you guys are using to protect yourselves from viruses and malicious hackers. I thought I'd just share with you guys and gals some of the info I've learned over the years. A couple of programs that I would highly recommend to you guys include Black Ice defender, which is a excellent Firewall program. What this does is blocks other users from connecting to your machine and attempting to exploit a trojan or and prevents them from gaining access to your files. My brother has been using the program for a couple of years now, and I used to bug him about it, asking why someone would select his machine and try and connect to his machine. After using his machine for an afternoon, and seeing how many people where scanning his machine (and he is using a dial up connection) I thought I should install it on my machine. I was shocked to see what was going on behind my back with my DSL connection to the net. Black Ice on average intercepts 100 attempts a day from users trying to scan my machine. The program automatically blocks these users. The other two programs that I would recommend is NeoTrace and Norton antivirus. Neotrace is very usefull for tracking users who are making repeated attempts to connect to your machine. This program works good with Black Ice as it gives you the IP address of the user who is attempting to hack into your machine, and you can enter this IP address into NeoTrace and it will trace it back and tell you who is messing with your machine. I had a user called CUTEGIRL who made repeated attempts to break into my machine, and using Neotrace I was able to track her down to the University of Indiana, and the program even gave me her computer station name, a satelite map of the city with the schools location, and the email and phone number of the head of security of the University. Very neat. Finally, as far as antivirus programs I find Norton antivirus to be the best out of any I've used. It seems to run quite unobtrusively in the background, and was the only virus checker that I was able to get rid of the CIH virus with. Hope this helps some of you out, later, <BR> <A HREF="http://www.networkice.com/products/blackice_defender.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.networkice.com/products/blackice_defender.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.neotrace.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.neotrace.com/</A> ||||reg||1
