Z||000002||Cheever2||01-16-2001||11:05 PM||||I just want something that watches every file or cookie that comes & goes, and takes care of it then & there, so I can be lazy and not run scans.  Sure I would have to get updates when available, but I don't want to find out I got a virus AFTER it has been in my machine a while.  I want it detected as soon as it shows up.  What will do that?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||01-16-2001||11:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>I just want something that watches every file or cookie that comes & goes, and takes care of it then & there, so I can be lazy and not run scans.  Sure I would have to get updates when available, but I don't want to find out I got a virus AFTER it has been in my machine a while.  I want it detected as soon as it shows up.  What will do that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>CookiePal does that... it's on download.com or winfiles.com<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
